\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Down Vs Yen, Dollar; Investors Stay Cautious\b0\par\par\uc2 By Frances McInnis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 902 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2010\par 22:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The euro fell against the dollar and yen Monday after concerns about the pace of global growth, exacerbated by disappointing euro-zone data, boosted the traditional safe harbors.\par \par \uc2 The yen was also stronger against the dollar, extending earlier gains made as investors speculated that Japanese officials may be further away from taking action to slow the yen's appreciation than previously thought.\par \par \uc2 With trading flows thin due to late-summer vacations, investors are guarded, said Ron Leven, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  in New York. The cautious mood weighed most heavily on the euro, which hit a near two-month low against the yen and a five-week low against the dollar, Leven said.\par \par \uc2 "The euro is the most vulnerable to a slowdown," Leven said. "The southern European countries that are going through all these somersaults trying to get their deficits down...won't get the tax revenues they were expecting."\par \par \uc2 After paring their anti-euro bets for six straight weeks, speculators increased their bets against the euro in the week ended Aug. 17, suggesting investors are becoming less supportive of the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Net speculative bets against the euro, called shorts, rose to 14,600 contracts with a value of $2.3 billion, from 3,700 contracts with a value of $595 million in the prior week, according to data, Friday from the Commodity Futures Trading Commission.\par \par \uc2 Late Monday, the euro was at $1.2665, down from $1.2706 late Friday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y85.25, below Y85.75. The euro weakened to Y107.95 from Y108.71, after falling as low as Y107.70. The U.K. pound was at $1.5520, up from $1.5490. The U.S. dollar advanced to CHF1.0405 from CHF1.0375.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 83.143 from 82.437.\par \par \uc2 To see the euro's performance against the dollar, please see:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4474"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4474}}}\par \par \uc2 To see the euro's performance against the yen, please see:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4475"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4475}}}\par \par \uc2 The euro's performance was further hampered by data showing the region's private sector expanded at a slower pace in August, weighed down by both the manufacturing and services sectors.\par \par \uc2 The disappointing data came after comments on Friday by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Axel Weber--usually seen to be one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most conservative members--who said the ECB should offer unlimited liquidity for Europe's banks into 2011.\par \par \uc2 The euro's struggles are "a lingering legacy" of the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis, said Daragh Maher, deputy head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Credit Agricole CIB in London. Fears are increasing that the severe austerity measures put in place to combat soaring deficits in some euro-zone countries will negatively affect growth in the region.\par \par \uc2 Despite the generally downbeat tone in markets, the Swiss franc, which also often functions as a safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was down against both the dollar and the euro. \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  President \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2  reiterated in a newspaper interview Saturday that preserving price stability remains the bank's main goal. Hildebrand noted that should deflation again become a threat, the bank could certainly act to prevent a further appreciation of the franc.\par \par \uc2 The SNB began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets in March 2009 to hinder the franc's strengthening against the euro, spending billions of francs to buy the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The SNB is believed to have halted its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June. The euro's all-time low is at CHF1.3072 and it traded at CHF1.3182 in New York Monday.\par \par \uc2 Investors also questioned the likelihood of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese officials after a Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  representative said that Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa didn't discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures during a much-anticipated phone conversation Monday. Many analysts and investors viewed the dialogue as indicating a lower degree of government pressure on the BOJ than had been expected.\par \par \uc2 Last week, several local media outlets reported the officials may meet in person as early as Monday, fueling speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might ease monetary policy or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to combat recent yen strength, which hurts the country's export-driven economy.\par \par \uc2 News that Australia's general election over the weekend failed to deliver a clear winner sent the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plummeting, but the Australian dollar had pared its losses by New York session.\par \par \uc2 "The uncertainty following the Australian election is likely to cause some near-term volatility," said analysts at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 , adding a coalition government involving the Green party would heighten fears of a mining tax and put the Australian dollar under pressure.\par \par \uc2 With the ICE Dollar Index strengthening, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 's PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bearish exchange-traded fund was down 0.19% from late Friday, while its PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bullish was up 0.21%. The two exchange-traded funds are based on \uc2 Deutsche Bank\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures indexes, whose composition mirrors that of the ICE's Dollar Index.\par \par \uc2 -By Frances McInnis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-3417; frances.mcinnis@dowjones.com [ 08-23-10 1632ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100823e68n000by\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
