\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Up Vs Higher-Yielding Rivals As US Stocks Tank\b0\par\par\uc2 By Frances McInnis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2010\par 22:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar gained against the euro and most other higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday after deepening fears about the country's slow pace of recovery sent investors to traditional safe harbors.\par \par \uc2 Disappointing U.S. employment and manufacturing data weighed on U.S. equity markets and led to losses for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely tied to global growth, such as the Australian, New Zealand and Canadian dollars.\par \par \uc2 "In general, there's a lack of conviction" in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, as poor U.S. data has investors wondering whether further deterioration in the U.S. economy is ahead, said Alvise Marino, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are unwilling to pile into positions, until they see where the economy is going," he said.\par \par \uc2 Low summer trading volumes may have exacerbated intraday \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, the euro was at $1.2820 from $1.2860 late Wednesday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y85.29 from Y85.43 after falling as low as Y84.89. The euro was at Y109.40 from Y109.87. The U.K. pound was at $1.5606 from $1.5605. The dollar was at CHF1.0325 from CHF1.0420.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 82.437 from 82.259.\par \par \uc2 To see the euro's performance against the dollar, please see:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4458"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4458}}}\par \par \uc2 The Philadelphia Fed index fell to -7.7 in August compared to 5.1 in July, and economists' expectations of a 7.0 reading.\par \par \uc2 U.S. initial unemployment claims also disappointed, rising by 12,000 to 500,000 in the week ended Aug. 14. It was the highest level since Nov. 14, and further stoked fears about the country's already weak labor market.\par \par \uc2 The rise in claims was particularly troubling because, with no seasonal factors affecting the week's results, economists had expected to see a decline. In previous weeks, analysts said data were likely distorted by seasonal adjustment factors tied to factory shutdowns by car makers and the hiring and firing of temporary workers for the 2010 Census.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian, Australian and New Zealand dollars all fell following the release of the data. Regional factors such as weak wholesale sales in Canada, rising input prices in New Zealand and the news that Fitch Ratings and Standard and Poor's placed mining giant BHP Billiton's A+ rating on watch also weighed on the commodity-backed dollar bloc.\par \par \uc2 The greenback's losses against the yen after the U.S. data were likely limited by talk of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the appreciation of the yen that is causing alarm among Japanese exporters, said Hidetoshi Yanagihara, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "Everybody will think about the possibility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said, noting there has been no clear signal from Japanese authorities on future action.\par \par \uc2 Still, speculation continues that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets or ease monetary policy should the yen rise further or government pressure increase.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the Malaysian ringgit surged to a near 13-year high and may scale new heights in the next few months after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules further by allowing companies to use the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to settle international trade, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Adding fresh impetus to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move, China started trading the Malaysian ringgit against the yuan on its domestic interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday, as part of its efforts to internationalize the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and boost cross-border trade.\par \par \uc2 With the ICE Dollar Index strengthening, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 's PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bearish exchange-traded fund was down 0.19% from late Wednesday, while its PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bullish was up 0.21%. The two exchange-traded funds are based on \uc2 Deutsche Bank\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures indexes, whose composition mirrors that of the ICE's Dollar Index.\par \par \uc2 -By Frances McInnis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-3417; frances.mcinnis@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Elffie Chew in Kuala Lumpur contributed to this article.) [ 08-19-10 1628ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100819e68j000cw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
