\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Gains Vs Yen, Falls Vs Euro As Risk Returns\b0\par\par\uc2 By Frances McInnis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 741 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2010\par 19:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar rose modestly against the yen but fell against the euro Tuesday as better-than-expected U.S. industrial data lifted the mood in markets.\par \par \uc2 The euro also gained against the traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  safe harbors, the dollar, yen and Swiss franc, after strong demand as Irish and Spanish government bond auctions soothed concerns about the ability of countries at the periphery of the euro zone to recapitalize.\par \par \uc2 A number of factors played into the revived demand for risk, said Matthew Strauss, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in Toronto. The European sovereign bond auctions and U.S. industrial production data, along with rallies in equity and commodity markets, all helped buoy investor sentiment, he said.\par \par \uc2 "It was enough for a market looking for good news," said Strauss.\par \par \uc2 Separately, investors were carefully watching the dollar's movements against the yen amid speculation that Japanese officials may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to combat recent yen strength. This caution effectively pinned the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a narrow range.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday afternoon, the euro was at $1.2881 from $1.2818 late Monday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y85.55 from Y85.30, while the euro was at Y110.19 from Y109.35. The U.K. pound was at $1.5577 from $1.5654. The U.S. dollar was at CHF1.0430 from CHF1.0397.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 82.207 from 82.470.\par \par \uc2 U.S. industrial production rebounded in July after a slight dip the previous month, in a reassuring sign from a segment of the economy that has helped drive the recovery. Manufacturing has been a key area of support for the economy as other segments such as consumer spending have showed signs of weakening.\par \par \uc2 U.S. housing starts also increased in July, while an index of producer prices matched economists' forecasts for a slight increase.\par \par \uc2 The industrial production numbers were "the first positive surprise in over a month of consistently disappointing U.S. data," said Michael Woolfolk, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNY Mellon in New York.\par \par \uc2 The data helped U.S. equities to rally and also helped the euro to hold onto its gains against traditional safe harbors like the dollar and yen, he said. Other higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Canadian and Australian dollars, also gained against the greenback as stock markets rallied.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Ireland sold the maximum intended EUR1.5 billion in government bonds at an auction Tuesday, which reassured markets that demand remains strong for high-yielding European sovereign bonds. A successful Spanish government bond auction drove home the message.\par \par \uc2 Irish bond prices have come under renewed pressure recently. Last week, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought short-dated Irish government bonds in an effort to investors nervous about the country's banks' ability to recapitalize.\par \par \uc2 The euro's gains on the auction news were tempered by a report that expectations for Germany's economy fell sharply in August, according to a closely-watched survey by the ZEW economic research institute.\par \par \uc2 "The German ZEW disappointed miserably, hinting that strong [second quarter] growth is unlikely to be repeated," wrote analysts from Scotia Capital in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Still, the extremely buoyant spring and summer were reflected in the strongest ever monthly rise in the subindex that tracks current conditions.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, investors continued to wonder whether Japanese officials would move to tackle the yen's recent strength.\par \par \uc2 Local media reported that Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan and Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa will meet Monday and are expected to discuss what to do about the yen, which is trading near 15-year highs against the dollar. Speculation is mounting that politicians, fearing that the yen's rise will hurt Japan's fragile, export-led recovery, might pressure the BOJ to ease policy further to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 However, a former senior Finance Ministry official said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  now to curb the yen's rise but may do so if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves become rapid.\par \par \uc2 -By Frances McInnis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-3417; frances.mcinnis@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Miho Nakauchi in Tokyo and Geoffrey T. Smith in Mannheim, Germany, contributed to this article) [ 08-17-10 1321ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100817e68h000as\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
