\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For August 13\b0\par\par\uc2 1,707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2010\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BOJ BOARD CONCERNED ABOUT YEN RISE, STOCK FALL IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan policy board members were already concerned about the steep rise in the yen and weakness in Tokyo shares at their July meeting, according to minutes released Friday. This has added to market speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may further ease monetary policy to curb the yen's strength. (published 0232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ 2Q RETAIL SALES OUTSTRIP EXPECTATIONS, DISCOUNTS PLAY A ROLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand retail sales far outstripped expectations in the second quarter, potentially paving the way for another rate hike by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at its September review, although economists point to heavy discounting and a pending rise in the Goods and Services Tax as contributing to the surprise result. (published 0310 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ HOUSE PRICES EASE AMID PATCHY ECONOMIC RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand home prices eased slightly in July from June, data from the Real Estate Institute of New Zealand showed Friday, confirming the housing market remains subdued, a trend that reduces impetus for the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to continue raising interest rates, at least in the short term. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN 2Q SMALL, MEDIUM SIZED-BUSINESS CONDITIONS DECLINE -NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business conditions for small to medium-sized business in Australia fell broadly in the second quarter, according to an industry survey released Friday. (published 2348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: CHINA, TAIWAN SHOULD CONSIDER \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SWAP PACT - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said China and Taiwan should use the Chinese yuan as the settlement \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for cross-strait trade, and central banks on both sides should consider signing a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap agreement, the Commercial Times reported Friday. (published 0040 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA 2Q ACTUAL MONTHLY HOUSEHOLD INCOME RISES FASTEST IN 3.5 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's actual household income in the second quarter grew at its fastest pace in three and a half years, as better economic conditions and robust exports more than offset a fall in asset income, Statistics Korea said Friday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALLIANCE GLOBAL: RAISED $500M VIA 7-YEAR BOND AT 6.625% YIELD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alliance Global Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has raised $500 million via its wholly-owned finance unit's offer of seven-year bonds, priced to yield 6.625%. (published 0126 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE TREASURY: NO PLAN YET TO UP RETAIL BOND ISSUE SIZE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the strong demand for the Philippine's retail treasury bond, National Treasurer Roberto Tan said Friday the government has yet to decide whether it will sell more than the amount it has planned. (published 0533 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE TREASURY CANCELS 5-YEAR BOND AUCTION TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine National Treasury said Friday it has cancelled an auction of PHP8.5 billion worth of five-year treasury bonds scheduled for next Tuesday. (published 0220 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN FINANCE MINISTRY CANCELS NT$20 BLN 182-DAY T-BILL SALE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's Finance Ministry said Friday it decided to cancel the sale of NT$20 billion worth of 182-day Treasury bills originally scheduled to take place on Aug. 20 because it has sufficient funds in the treasury. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =FOCUS: AUSTRALIA OPPOSITION BLOC VOWS TO REPAIR CHINA TIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's main opposition bloc is vowing to re-engage key Asian trade partners, especially China--upset by a series of diplomatic dust-ups last year--if it wins next weekend's federal election. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: SINGAPORE EXPORTS LIKELY GREW 20% ON YEAR IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's exports probably continued to grow in the double digits from last year for the eighth straight month in July, though the pace of expansion likely slowed amid a faltering global economic recovery. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: US EYES ARE ON CHINA, SO JAPAN'S ALONE OVER YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The last time the dollar dropped below the levels it reached Wednesday against the yen, the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Federal Reserve jointly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to push it higher. That was in July 1995. (published 2112 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS:DOLLAR/YEN OPTIONS DOWN;SPOT RISES TO Y86-LEVELS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options declined slightly in Asia Friday as the underlying exchange rate rose to around the Y86.00 level, reducing demand for hedges against the dollar's declines. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: WILMAR 2Q NET PROFIT FALLS 15.4% TO US$344.5 MILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wilmar International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's biggest palm oil trader by volume, unexpectedly reported a 15.4% decline in its second quarter net profit after it accounted for decreased valuation of convertible bonds and margins fell. (published 2356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TELSTRA STRIKES DEAL WITH PRIVATE EQUITY FIRMS ON SOUFUN IPO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telstra Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has struck a deal with two private equity firms that will see it exit its 51% stake in Chinese real estate advertising website \f28 \uc2 \f2 SouFun Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . as it gears up for an initial public offer. (published 0016 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 KOREAN AIR\f28 \uc2 \f2  POSTS 2Q NET LOSS DUE TO HIGH COSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A stronger local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which escalated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses and non-operating costs, pushed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korean Air Lines Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . into the red in the second quarter, but the airline was upbeat as it inked a record high operating profit as more people travelled abroad amid an economic recovery. (published 0444 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KOREA LIFE INSURANCE\f28 \uc2 \f2  1Q NET KRW128.52 BLN VS KRW5.62 BLN NET LOSS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Life Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday said it swung to a net profit for the fiscal first quarter. (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SSANGYONG 2Q NET LOSS NARROWS TO KRW21.54 BLN ON IMPROVED SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ssangyong Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that its net losses narrowed to KRW21.54 billion in the second quarter from KRW177.17 billion a year earlier as the revival of the economy helped improve sales. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LI KA-SHING RAISES HUTCHISON WHAMPOA STAKE TO 52.28% VS 51.92% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tycoon \f28 \uc2 \f2 Li Ka-shing\f28 \uc2 \f2  has raised his stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hutchison Whampoa Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to 52.28% from 51.92%, according to disclosures filed to the Hong Kong stock exchange. (published 0044 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASUSTEK SWINGS TO 2ND-QUARTER NET PROFIT OF NT$3.32 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asustek Computer Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a personal computer maker and the world's biggest motherboard producer by shipments, said Friday it swung to a second-quarter net profit of NT$3.32 billion from a NT$131 million net loss a year earlier because of a jump in revenue. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHIMAO PROPERTY: SHANGHAI UNIT'S 1ST-HALF NET PROFIT SURGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shimao Property Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its Shanghai-listed unit posted a more than eight-fold rise in first-half net profit because of higher sales of commercial projects. (published 0143 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TRANSFIELD SERVICES: A$200M OF WORK WITH AUSTRALIAN RAIL TRACK CORP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transfield Services Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has won rail infrastructure work worth A$200 million over the next two years with the Australian government. (published 0004 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PGG WRIGHTSON SWUNG TO PROFIT LAST FY, BUT DOWNBEAT ABOUT RURAL SECTOR CONDITIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rural services provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 PGG Wrightson Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . returned to profit for the fiscal year ended June 30 after a heavy loss the previous year, but remains downbeat about conditions in the rural sector. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AYALA CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  2Q NET PROFIT UP 21% AT PHP2.3 BLN ON AFFILIATES' EARNINGS CONTRIBUTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ayala Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that second-quarter net profit increased 21% from a year earlier, bolstered by the robust performance of its real estate, banking, water utility, automotive, business process outsourcing and semiconductor businesses. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PACIFIC & ORIENT GETS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  APPROVAL TO START TALKS ON SALE OF UNIT TO PRUDENTIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pacific & Orient Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that it has received approval from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to commence talks to sell a stake in its non-life insurance unit Pacific & Orient Insurance Co. to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Prudential Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . part of U.K. insurer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Prudential PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  . (published 0508 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHIPPING CORP OF INDIA\f28 \uc2 \f2  INVITES BIDS FROM MERCHANT BANKS FOR PROPOSED FPO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shipping Corp. of India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday invited bids from investment banks interested in arranging its proposed follow-on public offer, in which both the federal government and the company will each offer a 10% stake. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITIGROUP TO ADD AT LEAST 130 STAFF TO ASIA SECURITIES, FUND SERVICES UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citigroup Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s securities and fund services unit in Asia plans to expand its staff of 1,300 by 10% to 12% over the next 12 months as the region's asset management industry grows quickly. (published 0348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TIMAH 1H NET PROFIT IDR314 BLN VS IDR37.5 BLN - MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tin miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Timah\f28 \uc2 \f2 's first-half net profit grew to IDR314 billion from IDR37.5 billion in the same period a year earlier due to higher sales and commodity prices, State-Enterprise Minister Mustafa Abubakar told reporters Friday. (published 0652 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; YEN CONCERNS CAP TOKYO GAINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most Asian share markets were moderately higher on Friday after recent losses, but uncertainty over whether Japanese authorities will act to curb the yen's recent strength curtailed gains on the Tokyo market. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA COMMISSION: WHEAT PRICE RALLY LIKELY LIMITED DUE TO STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global wheat price increases are likely to be limited by historically high levels of global stocks and relatively high output expectations this year, despite the drought in the Black Sea area, China's top economic planning agency said. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NZX SEEKS TO DEVELOP WHOLE MILK POWDER FUTURES MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 13-08-10 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand Stock Exchange said Friday it is seeking Market Makers for its first Whole Milk Powder Futures contract. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PETROCHINA RESUMES PRODUCTION AT 12% OF LIAOHE WELLS AFTER FLOODING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has resumed production at about 12% of the wells in its Liaohe oil field that were shut down in past weeks due to flooding, parent \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday in its inhouse newsletter. (published 0336 GMT) [ 13-08-10 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100813e68d000j9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
