\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2010\par 09:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN 2Q GDP GREW AT FASTEST PACE IN 20 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The German economy grew at its fastest pace since reunification in 1990 in the second quarter of the year, thanks to strong contributions from exports and investment, the Federal Statistics Office, Destatis, reported Friday. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH FINANCE MINISTER: 2Q GDP +0.6%; 1Q REVISED UP TO +0.2% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French finance minister Christine Lagarde Friday said gross domestic product grew 0.6% in the second quarter from the previous three months. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH CONSUMER PRICES DECLINE 0.3% IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French consumer prices declined slightly in July after remaining stable in June, the country's statistics office said Friday. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPANISH 2Q GDP +0.2% ON QUARTER, -0.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Spanish economy grew 0.2% in the second quarter from the first quarter, extending modest gains after a long period of economic contraction, according to preliminary data from the National Statistics Institute released Friday. (published 0700 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ BOARD CONCERNED ABOUT YEN RISE, STOCK FALL IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan policy board members were already concerned about the steep rise in the yen and weakness in Tokyo shares at their July meeting, according to minutes released Friday. This has added to market speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may further ease monetary policy to curb the yen's strength. (published 0232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN 2Q SMALL, MEDIUM SIZED-BUSINESS CONDITIONS DECLINE -NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business conditions for small to medium-sized business in Australia fell broadly in the second quarter, according to an industry survey released Friday. (published 2348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: CHINA, TAIWAN SHOULD CONSIDER \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SWAP PACT - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said China and Taiwan should use the Chinese yuan as the settlement \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for cross-strait trade, and central banks on both sides should consider signing a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap agreement, the Commercial Times reported Friday. (published 0040 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA 2Q ACTUAL MONTHLY HOUSEHOLD INCOME RISES FASTEST IN 3.5 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's actual household income in the second quarter grew at its fastest pace in three and a half years, as better economic conditions and robust exports more than offset a fall in asset income, Statistics Korea said Friday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : YEN DOWN VS DOLLAR, BUT MAY RISE AGAIN IF US DATA WEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen fell against the dollar in Asia Friday after Japanese officials hardened the tone of their comments on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, but dealers said the safe-haven yen could rise sharply later in the global day if upcoming U.S. data deepen concerns about the health of the country's economy. (published 0601 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN EQUITY INDEX TECHNICALS: SEEN REBOUNDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday DAX: The false breakout of the 6125 mark calls for a tentative rebound. Suggest long positions above 6065 with 6216 and 6260 in sight. The downside breakout of 6065 will open the way to 6000 and 5975. (published 0642 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: UP MOVES EYED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The contracts remain on the upside but should pull back before further up moves. (published 0749 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOCUS: AUSTRALIA OPPOSITION BLOC VOWS TO REPAIR CHINA TIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's main opposition bloc is vowing to re-engage key Asian trade partners, especially China--upset by a series of diplomatic dust-ups last year--if it wins next weekend's federal election. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MONEY TALKS: US EYES ARE ON CHINA, SO JAPAN'S ALONE OVER YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The last time the dollar dropped below the levels it reached Wednesday against the yen, the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Federal Reserve jointly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to push it higher. That was in July 1995. (published 2112 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS:DOLLAR/YEN OPTIONS DOWN;SPOT RISES TO Y86-LEVELS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options declined slightly in Asia Friday as the underlying exchange rate rose to around the Y86.00 level, reducing demand for hedges against the dollar's declines. (published 0438 GMT) [ 13-08-10 0703GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100813e68d000iy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
