\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2010\par 07:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BOJ BOARD CONCERNED ABOUT YEN RISE, STOCK FALL IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan policy board members were already concerned about the steep rise in the yen and weakness in Tokyo shares at their July meeting, according to minutes released Friday. This has added to market speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may further ease monetary policy to curb the yen's strength. (published 0232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ 2Q RETAIL SALES OUTSTRIP EXPECTATIONS, DISCOUNTS PLAY A ROLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand retail sales far outstripped expectations in the second quarter, potentially paving the way for another rate hike by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at its September review, although economists point to heavy discounting and a pending rise in the Goods and Services Tax as contributing to the surprise result. (published 0310 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ HOUSE PRICES EASE AMID PATCHY ECONOMIC RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand home prices eased slightly in July from June, data from the Real Estate Institute of New Zealand showed Friday, confirming the housing market remains subdued, a trend that reduces impetus for the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to continue raising interest rates, at least in the short term. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN 2Q SMALL, MEDIUM SIZED-BUSINESS CONDITIONS DECLINE -NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business conditions for small to medium-sized business in Australia fell broadly in the second quarter, according to an industry survey released Friday. (published 2348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: CHINA, TAIWAN SHOULD CONSIDER \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SWAP PACT - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said China and Taiwan should use the Chinese yuan as the settlement \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for cross-strait trade, and central banks on both sides should consider signing a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap agreement, the Commercial Times reported Friday. (published 0040 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA 2Q ACTUAL MONTHLY HOUSEHOLD INCOME RISES FASTEST IN 3.5 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's actual household income in the second quarter grew at its fastest pace in three and a half years, as better economic conditions and robust exports more than offset a fall in asset income, Statistics Korea said Friday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ALLIANCE GLOBAL: RAISED $500M VIA 7-YEAR BOND AT 6.625% YIELD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alliance Global Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has raised $500 million via its wholly-owned finance unit's offer of seven-year bonds, priced to yield 6.625%. (published 0126 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE TREASURY CANCELS 5-YEAR BOND AUCTION TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine National Treasury said Friday it has cancelled an auction of PHP8.5 billion worth of five-year treasury bonds scheduled for next Tuesday. (published 0220 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TAIWAN FINANCE MINISTRY CANCELS NT$20 BLN 182-DAY T-BILL SALE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's Finance Ministry said Friday it decided to cancel the sale of NT$20 billion worth of 182-day Treasury bills originally scheduled to take place on Aug. 20 because it has sufficient funds in the treasury. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par =PREVIEW: SINGAPORE EXPORTS LIKELY GREW 20% ON YEAR IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's exports probably continued to grow in the double digits from last year for the eighth straight month in July, though the pace of expansion likely slowed amid a faltering global economic recovery. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: US EYES ARE ON CHINA, SO JAPAN'S ALONE OVER YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The last time the dollar dropped below the levels it reached Wednesday against the yen, the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Federal Reserve jointly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to push it higher. That was in July 1995. (published 2112 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS:DOLLAR/YEN OPTIONS DOWN;SPOT RISES TO Y86-LEVELS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options declined slightly in Asia Friday as the underlying exchange rate rose to around the Y86.00 level, reducing demand for hedges against the dollar's declines. (published 0438 GMT) [ 13-08-10 0501GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100813e68d000a9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
