\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Russia Drought To Accelerate Inflation -\uc2 Unicredit\b0\par\par\uc2 1,345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2010\par 10:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0825 GMT [Dow Jones]--Forest fires and Russia's worst drought in decades are causing an acceleration in the country's consumer price index, which rose to 0.2% week-on-week in the period to Aug. 9 after almost three straight months of 0.1% weekly growth, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Unicredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. The acceleration took place due to the impact of severe drought in key food-producing regions, which will likely spur further growth in inflation this year, the bank says. Russia's CPI stands at 5.0% for the year. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0824 GMT [Dow Jones] Swedish July CPI, at -0.3% on the month and +1.1% on the year was slightly higher than SEB's forecast of -0.4% and +1.0%, but slightly below consensus, explained by seasonally normal price decreases for clothing and lower petrol prices, the bank says. CPI excluding interest costs, CPIF, rose 1.7% on the year, down from 1.9% in June. "The lower Y/Y change for CPIF is explained by lower core (excluding energy and food) inflation, which supports our forecast that CPIF is in a downward trend," SEB says. EUR/SEK trades at 9.4671. (ian.edmondson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0821 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex turns up, +0.1% at 18,079.46 vs session-low of 17,914.78, on strong results from heavyweight \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2  (500112.BY), which +4.7% at INR2,725.25. SBI's stock hits all-time high of INR2,735.85 after lender posts 1Q net profit +25.1% on-year at INR29.14 billion vs INR25.07 billion average forecast in Dow Jones poll of 12 analysts. "This is another indication that there is nothing fundamentally wrong with the Indian markets. Given the rally we have seen lately (Sensex up over 5% in 3 months), there might be some correction, but nothing worrisome," says Kunal Dalal, head of research at KRC Research. Adds valuations aren't unduly expensive as even at 18,500-levels, Sensex would trade at about 18X on FY11 earnings estimate of INR1,030. other major gainers include Oil & Natural Gas (500312.BY), +2.4% at INR1,266, and \uc2 Hindustan Unilever\uc2  (500696.BY), +2.1% at INR265.70. S&P CNX Nifty flat at 5422.35. (shikhar.balwani@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0819 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian government bond prices continue sliding on resurfacing risk aversion around the globe, dealers say. "The rupiah's slide against the dollar triggered selling on the government bonds," a dealer says; adds foreigners likely to continue trimming bond holdings Friday if risk appetite continues deteriorating; 10-year yield up at 8.09% vs 7.97% yesterday; 15-year yield at 8.61% vs 8.45%; 20-year yield up at 9.07% vs 8.90%. USD/IDR up at 9,000 vs 8,975 late yesterday. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0819 GMT [Dow Jones] More verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and price checking by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has driven the USD a little higher against the JPY. However, the USD is mostly lower elsewhere as investors appear to take profits on the sharp rally staged after the FOMC decided to preserve liquidity levels Tuesday. The improvement in general sentiment helped European stocks push into positive territory even though Asian stocks were lower. The USD is up at Y85.63 after dipping down to Y84.94 earlier. The EUR is up at $1.2921 as the market now waits for the latest euro zone industrial production data. The GBP is also up a little at $1.5694. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0816 GMT [Dow Jones] China's efforts to hold down the yuan are making life even tougher for the Japanese authorities, which are squaring up to painful yen strength. China's yuan-management program is indirectly pushing even greater inflows into the yen, as it's the only regional heavy-hitter left to take the strain, says Lutz Karpowitz at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already stepped up the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, and Karpowitz reckons a real \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "cannot be ruled out" at this point. USD/JPY trades higher on these concerns, at Y85.62. (katie.martin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0809 GMT [Dow Jones] The AUD has been a major casualty of the USD rally, and it, as well as other commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , looks set to suffer more as global growth concerns rise. "The AUD/USD has broken below its 200-day moving average which is likely to generate selling interest among portfolio managers, with AUD/JPY already breaking lower from its recent trading range," the bank notes. AUD/USD trades at 0.8987, AUD/JPY at 76.97. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0807 GMT [Dow Jones] A worrying aspect of the global growth slowdown is that the recent improvement in labor markets is stalling worldwide, says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . "While this is most evident in the U.S. labour market, conditions seen recently in Canada, UK and even the Australian labour market report overnight, point to some worrying trends," the bank says. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0759 GMT [Dow Jones] The Turkish lira and bonds are flat in line with mixed global stock markets and a flat Istanbul Stock Exchange. USD/TRY trades at 1.5190, unchanged from Wednesday. The benchmark April 25, 2012 bond trades at 8.44%, unchanged from Wednesday. Analysts forecast TRY to trade between 1.5130 and 1.5260, and the benchmark bond to trade between 8.30% and 8.50%, in the short term.\par \par \uc2 0754 GMT [Dow Jones] Augus