\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Japan PM, BOJ governor may meet next week on yen\b0\par\par\uc2 798 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2010\par 00:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 *\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  ramping up verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt yen rise\par \par \uc2 *Traders say yen may keep rising as \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely\par \par \uc2 *Yen has retreated slightly from 15-year high vs dollar\par \par \uc2 *Democrat backbenchers say govt should consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Adds details on lawmakers' proposal, GDP forecast)\par \par \uc2 By Stanley White and Masayuki Kitano\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 13 (Reuters) - Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan and Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa may meet as early as next week to discuss the yen's strength and possible responses, although likely options are seen as limited.\par \par \uc2 Japanese policymakers have been trying to talk the yen down this week as it surged to a 15-year high against the dollar, and the government and the BOJ are now coordinating to set up a meeting between Kan and Shirakawa that will likely take place in the second half of next week, government sources said.\par \par \uc2 Shirakawa has met Japanese prime ministers before but this meeting is expected to focus on the yen's gains, which Tokyo worries will derail a fragile economic recovery and exacerbate deflation.\par \par \uc2 But traders said the yen was still likely to gain longer term, because Group of Seven countries are unlikely to agree to joint \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their own economies are not recovering strongly.\par \par \uc2 "It's really hard to answer the question why other countries have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  just for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are falling due to a weak economic outlook," said Tsutomu Soma, senior manager of foreign securities at \uc2 Okasan Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar edged higher on Friday and was around 85.75 yen by late afternoon in Tokyo, more than a yen above Wednesday's 15-year low of 84.72, on the prospect that Japanese officials will increase verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to stem yen gains.\par \par \uc2 "This is an opportunity to cover some short (dollar) positions, but traders are likely to continue to target a break of 80 yen," Soma said.\par \par \uc2 VOLLEY OF COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 A group of junior lawmakers in the ruling Democratic Party called on the government and the BOJ to use \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and quantitative easing to bring the yen toward 110 per dollar, Yoichi Kaneko, a leading member of the group, said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The group has made similar proposals in the past, but the government has not reflected its ideas in policy decisions.\par \par \uc2 Japan policymakers fired off a volley of comments on Thursday to curb yen strength and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  checked rates with banks as officials stepped up efforts to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from harming the economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The economy's growth likely slowed to 0.6 percent in April-June from a 1.2 percent expansion in the previous quarter as export growth moderated and the boost to consumer spending from government incentives faded, a Reuters poll of economists showed. The data is due on Aug. 16.\par \par \uc2 The yen has risen steadily against the dollar since early May, gaining more than 10 percent and closing in on its 1995 record high of 79.75 per dollar, fuelling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities have not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect exporters from a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since March 2004, when a 15-month yen selling spree came to an end.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen as difficult, whether jointly with other countries or alone, although market players say the chance of solo action increases the closer the yen gets to 80 per dollar and if its rise accelerates to a pace of 2 to 3 yen per day.\par \par \uc2 The other wild card is the Nikkei share average. Market players say a steep drop in the stock market benchmark would also alarm authorities and could be another catalyst for action.\par \par \uc2 Other options include policy steps by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as expanding a funding \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched last December to pump more cash into the banking system, which is seen as the most likely option, or buying more government bonds.\par \par \uc2 Japanese manufacturers' confidence rose to the highest in nearly three years in August due to government stimulus, but companies forecast for the first time in three years that their sentiment will deteriorate as the strong yen threatens exporters' earnings, a Reuters poll showed.\par \par \uc2 Some BOJ board members believe there is a need to watch the impact of the yen's rise and the stock market decline on the economy, minutes of the bank's July 14-15 meeting showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Some members also said the yen had appreciated in part because investors had no better alternative than to buy yen as safe assets. (Writing by Stanley White, additional reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100812e68c001tq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
