\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2010\par 15:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par US JOBLESS CLAIMS RISE 2K IN WEEK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of U.S. workers making new claims for jobless benefits unexpectedly climbs by 2,000 to 484,000 in the week ended Aug. 7, adding to concerns about the economy's weakness.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US IMPORT PRICES RISE 0.2% IN JULY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. import prices bounce back slightly after dropping in June, driven by a 2.1% rise in fuel import prices and higher food prices, a move that could help ease deflation concerns. The increase is less than the 0.4% increase economists were expecting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GM POSTS $1.3B PROFIT, LARGEST SINCE 2004 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Auto giant's 2Q profit is driven by improving sales in every region except Europe and sharply lower expenses due to last year's bankruptcy. Revenue surges 43% to $33 billion, while global production grows 50%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREEK RECESSION DEEPENS, UNEMPLOYMENT HIGH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Greek economy contracts sharply in the 2Q as government austerity measures bite deeper into incomes, according to government data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB SAYS PRIVATE DEMAND KEY TO TRADE RECOVERY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Healthier banks and more private-sector demand are necessary if the euro zone, and the world economy in general, is to continue its recovery, the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EXPERTS FORECAST HIGHER LONG-TERM CPI SAY ECB \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Experts in a quarterly poll by the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expect inflation beyond the medium term to be somewhat higher than in the previous survey, the ECB says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES DROP AS US JOBLESS CLAIMS RISE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock futures extend losses after U.S. weekly jobless claims rise by 2,000 to 484,000. Disappointing industrial production in the euro zone is adding to investors' concerns about the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN UTILITIES WARN ON FUEL TAX EFFECTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany's plan to tax the fuel used to fire nuclear power plants could make reactors unprofitable and hasten the country's exit from atomic energy generation, the country's leading utilities warn.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NO CHANGE IN BOJ'S MONETARY STANCE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Senior Bank Of Japan official Hiroshi Nakaso says that despite sharp rises in the yen and falls in Tokyo stock prices, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hasn't changed its monetary stance or economic assessment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANY BAA STRIKE WOULD 'DAMAGE' UK ECONOMY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. Prime Minister David Cameron says that he very much hopes a strike will be avoided at airport operator BAA and that industrial action will harm the U.K. economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Focus \par EURO-ZONE DEBT CRISIS COMES BACK TO HAUNT EURO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro-zone debt crisis is back on the agenda in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets as the euro takes a beating against the dollar and other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , weighed down by strains in the region's bond markets and banks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Analysis \par YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNLIKELY DESPITE STRAINED NERVES \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is extremely unlikely to try and weaken the super-strong yen any time soon, despite its clear unease with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent climb, Katie Martin writes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interview \par LAS VEGAS SANDS STRUGGLES TO HIRE IN MACAU \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Las Vegas Sands\f28 \uc2 \f2  is struggling to find labor to complete a long-delayed $4 billion expansion project in Macau, the world's largest gambling market, and needs to up headcount at its Cotai project seven-fold to get the project done.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES FALL AS JOBLESS CLAIMS RISE; DJIA OFF 66 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US stock futures fall further as weekly US jobless claims rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 10-YEAR TREASURY ERASES DECLINE AFTER JOBLESS CLAIMS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys erase losses to trade little changed after unexpected rise in jobless claims.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DOLLAR FALLS DESPITE JAPANESE VERBAL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar eases after a brief rally, euro slips after industrial production figures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE FALLS FOR THIRD DAY AS ECONOMY FEARS WEIGH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude falls for third day as fears about the economy weigh on prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPOT GOLD EDGES UP AS INVESTOR DEMAND BUILDS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold edges up in Europe on improving investor, physical demand. [ 12-08-10 1300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100812e68c00164\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
