\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2010\par 14:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par GM SECURES CREDIT, CLEARS WAY FOR IPO FILING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Motors secures a $5 billion credit facility in a step that clears the way for its return to the public markets later this year, two people familiar with the deal tell The Wall Street Journal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB SAYS PRIVATE DEMAND KEY TO TRADE RECOVERY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Healthier banks and more private-sector demand are necessary if the euro zone, and the world economy in general, is to continue its recovery, the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EXPERTS FORECAST HIGHER LONG-TERM CPI SAY ECB \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Experts in a quarterly poll by the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expect inflation beyond the medium term to be somewhat higher than in the previous survey, the ECB says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NO CHANGE IN BOJ'S MONETARY STANCE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Senior Bank Of Japan official Hiroshi Nakaso says that despite sharp rises in the yen and falls in Tokyo stock prices, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hasn't changed its monetary stance or economic assessment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES DROP, CISCO WEIGHS ON TECHS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock futures extend losses after the previous session's rout, as a disappointing revenue outlook from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cisco\f28 \uc2 \f2  weighs on the technology sector. The aftermath of the Federal Reserve's meeting earlier this week is continuing to put pressure on equities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANY BAA STRIKE WOULD 'DAMAGE' UK ECONOMY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. Prime Minister David Cameron says that he very much hopes a strike will be avoided at airport operator BAA and that industrial action will harm the U.K. economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DANA, KNOC TAKEOVER TALKS BREAK DOWN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dana Petroleum\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares are sharply lower after the Scotland-based company says talks to be taken over by KNOC have broken down. They were unable to agree on terms to give the Korean company access to detailed financial information ahead of a formal bid.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PRUDENTIAL TOPS VIEWS, RAISES DIVIDEND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. insurer Prudential says it will focus on its organic growth strategy and ruled out putting up another bid for AIA, after reporting better-than-expected results.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S UPBEAT ON ASIA, SEES PRESSURE ON JAPAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says the trend for Asia-Pacific sovereign ratings is positive, though Japan's rating could come under pressure from any hesitation to cut its budget deficit or a renewed global economic slump.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO-ZONE INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT DROPS UNEXPECTEDLY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industrial production in the euro zone falls unexpectedly in June, as drops in output in France and Germany suggest the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area's economic recovery slowed at the end of the 2Q, official data shows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Analysis \par YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNLIKELY DESPITE STRAINED NERVES \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is extremely unlikely to try and weaken the super-strong yen any time soon, despite its clear unease with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent climb, Katie Martin writes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interview \par LAS VEGAS SANDS STRUGGLES TO HIRE IN MACAU \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Las Vegas Sands\f28 \uc2 \f2  is struggling to find labor to complete a long-delayed $4 billion expansion project in Macau, the world's largest gambling market, and needs to up headcount at its Cotai project seven-fold to get the project done.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par The Wall Street Journal \par SCHOOL SEASON NOT WHAT IT USED TO BE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Small retailers brace for another disappointing back-to-school season as a tougher credit environment, dismal consumer spending and competition from big-box stores further push some out of the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES DROP, CISCO OUTLOOK WEIGHS ON TECHS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US stock futures trade lower as Cicso's revenue weighs on technology sector.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TREASURYS LOWER AFTER RECENT SHARP GAINS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US Treasurys are lower as traders book profits.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DOLLAR FALLS DESPITE JAPANESE VERBAL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar eases after a brief rally, euro slips after industrial production figures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE FALLS FOR THIRD DAY AS ECONOMY FEARS WEIGH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude falls for third day as fears about the economy weigh on prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPOT GOLD EDGES UP AS INVESTOR DEMAND BUILDS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold edges up in Europe on improving investor, physical demand. [ 12-08-10 1200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100812e68c00146\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
