\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2010\par 12:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ NAKASO: NO CHANGE IN BOJ'S MONETARY STANCE, ECONOMIC VIEW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Senior Bank Of Japan official Hiroshi Nakaso said Thursday that despite sharp rises in the yen and falls in Tokyo stock prices, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hasn't changed its monetary stance or economic assessment. (published 0915 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: EURO-ZONE INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT DROPS UNEXPECTEDLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industrial production in the euro zone fell unexpectedly in June, as drops in output in France and Germany suggested the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area's economic recovery slowed at the end of the second quarter, official data showed Thursday. (published 0900 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB: EXPERTS FORECAST HIGHER LONG-TERM CPI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Experts in a quarterly poll by the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expect inflation beyond the medium term to be somewhat higher than in the previous survey, the ECB said Thursday. (published 0943 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER STEPS UP RHETORIC AGAINST RISING YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister escalated his warnings against the yen's rise Thursday, threatening to take "appropriate action" against the persistent rises for the first time since he took office in June. (published 0953 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB: STRESS TESTS UNDERSTATED BANKS' PROGRESS ON CAPITAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The results of stress tests conducted on 91 of the European Union's largest banks this summer tended to understate the progress made by banks in strengthening their balance sheets, the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  argued in its monthly report for August. (published 1044 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S: ASIA-PACIFIC SOVEREIGN RATINGS HEADING IN POSITIVE DIRECTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service Thursday said the trend for sovereign ratings in the Asia-Pacific region is a positive one, though Japan's rating could come under pressure from political instability. (published 0732 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN NODA: WATCHING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOVES WITH GREAT INTEREST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Thursday that the government will take appropriate action on the strong yen while watching \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market movements. (published 0940 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOVERNOR SHIRAKAWA: SEE LARGE MOVEMENT IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , SHARE MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Thursday he recognised "substantial fluctuations" in financial markets amid concerns over the strength of the U.S. economy. (published 0940 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB: NEED STRONGER PRIVATE DEMAND TO SUPPORT TRADE RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Healthier banks and more private-sector demand are necessary if the euro zone, and the world economy in general, is to continue its recovery, the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday in its monthly report for August. (published 0937 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREEK 2Q GDP -1.5% ON QUARTER, -3.5% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greek second quarter gross domestic product slumped 1.5% on a quarter-on-quarter basis, from a fall of 0.8% in the first quarter, the National Statistics Service said Thursday. (published 0910 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREECE MAY UNEMPLOYMENT 12.0% VS 11.9% IN APRIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Greek unemployment rate rose to 12.0% in May from 11.9% in April and was up sharply from 8.5% a year earlier, the National Statistics Service said Thursday. (published 0919 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ITALY JUNE WORLD TRADE DEFICIT WIDENS TO EUR3.05B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy's trade deficit with countries around the world widened in June on the year earlier, as imports rose more than exports, national statistics institute Istat said Thursday. (published 0908 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: ITALY JULY FINAL CPI +0.4% ON MO; +1.7% ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy's annual consumer price index continued to rise in July, reaching its highest level since December 2008, final data from statistics agency Istat confirmed Thursday. (published 0912 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPAIN JULY CPI ACCELERATES TO +1.9% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spanish consumer prices rose at a faster pace in July than in recent months, the result of price increases for food, beverages and energy products, Spain's National Statistics Institute, or INE, said in a statement Thursday. (published 0700 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA YUAN FALLS SHARPLY; CENTRAL PARITY SET AT 7-WEEK HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's yuan was sharply lower against the U.S. dollar Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the dollar-yuan central parity rate at a seven-week high following the U.S. unit's broad strength against most major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  overnight amid concerns about a weakening global economic recovery. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER XIA: YUAN'S WEAKNESS THURSDAY IS NORMAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan's decline Thursday is normal and the slowdown in China's economic growth is within expectations, a Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser said a day after a raft of July economic data showed easing growth in the world's third-largest economy. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF, BOJ OFFICIALS DISCUSS YEN IN SPECIAL MEETING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's most powerful \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bureaucrat held a special meeting with a senior Bank of Japan official Thursday to discuss market conditions such as the yen's strength, highlighting how concerned policymakers have become about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's growth-hurting upward trend. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK CML CUTS 2010 PROPERTY REPOSSESSION FORECAST AFTER 2Q DECLINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of U.K. homeowners having their property repossessed fell to its lowest in over two years in the second quarter, a mortgage industry body said Tuesday, adding that it is cutting its forecast for the full-year total of repossessions. (published 0900 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA PRIMARY ARTICLES WPI DOWN 0.1% IN WEEK TO JULY 31 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The wholesale price index for primary articles in India fell 0.1% to 308.0 in the week to July 31 from a provisional 308.2 in the previous week, showed data issued Thursday by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT GROWTH SLOWS AS BASE EFFECT ERODES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's industrial output in June grew 7.1% from a year earlier, decelerating sharply from eight months of double-digit expansion, as the effect of a weak base eroded and government spending slowed. (published 0728 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN JOBLESS RISE TO KEEP RBA SIDELINED UNTIL 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's unemployment rate rose sharply in July as aggressive interest rate hikes earlier in the year slow the economy. (published 0249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par MONEY TALKS: NEXT BIG YUAN MOVE MAY NOT COME BEFORE MID-2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's move to let the yuan weaken Thursday--setting the U.S. dollar daily central parity rate at a seven-week high--is another sign major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy change won't come this year. (published 0910 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR FALLS DESPITE JAPANESE VERBAL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The threat of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to halt the dollar falling under Y85 dominated trading Thursday, but after a brief rally the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  soon fell back again. (published 0917 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: RENEWED EURO-SELLING IS ON ITS WAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the FOMC now out of the way, the euro zone's problems are coming back into focus. (published 0715 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAKING STOCK: ASIAN TIGERS COULD BE GULF MARKETS' SAVIORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Don't write off the Persian Gulf stock markets just yet. Growing interest in the region from its Asian neighbors may still provide some much-needed support to faltering regional equities this year. (published 0725 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: USD TO CONSOLIDATE WED RALLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: the pair should post a rebound as the RSI is well directed. Suggest long positions above 1.283 with 1.2925 and 1.2985 in sight. The downside penetration of 1.283 will call for a slide towards 1.28 and 1.275. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: NO REVERSALS SEEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The contracts remain on the upside and do not show any signs of reversal. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR REBOUNDS VS YEN AS JAPAN OFFICIALS SHOW CONCERN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar rebounded against the yen in Asia Thursday after Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan expressed concern about recent movement in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, a day after the U.S. unit slid to a 15-year low against its Japanese counterpart. (published 0618 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN 2Q GDP GROWTH LIKELY SLOWED AS CONSUMPTION, EXPORTS LOSE STEAM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economic recovery slowed in the second quarter of 2010, data due out Monday is expected to show, as consumers bought fewer TVs and cars, while slowdowns in the U.S. and China kept a lid on export growth. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN CORRECTION, BUT SOME MAY HOLD GROUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to lose significant ground against the U.S. dollar in coming days on fears that a global slowdown will crimp demand in the developed world. But some -- like the Chinese yuan, Japanese yen and Hong Kong dollar -- may rise further. (published 0411 GMT) [ 12-08-10 1002GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100812e68c000yh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
